# Pages this directory has retired. `scripts/qa_maps.py` copies its whole
# output folder and never removes, so without this list every page deleted
# here comes back the next time anybody runs any part of that script — which
# is exactly what happened on 2026-09-12, when an unrelated run restored all
# 199 pages retired that morning.
#
# One shell glob per line, matched against the file name only.
# The reasoning for each group is docs/publication-inventory.md in the
# structure-loss-pipeline repository (ledger `pub-2026-09-12`).

# v1 Landsat damage maps: built through the read window road-7 fixed, and the
# product does not ship a Landsat damage model.
damage_*_landsat.html

# Pre-sampler-fix Sentinel-2 damage maps. Superseded by the _sentinel2_v4
# siblings, which are published.
damage_*_sentinel2.html

# The damage_sentinel2_v2 bundle: superseded by s1_v3, then s1_v4, then v5.
damage_*_sentinel2_v2.html

# Pre-sampler-fix Stage-7 out-of-sample checks.
dins_*.html

# Stage-3 detection maps from a detector two versions behind the frozen one.
detections_*.html

# (The two legacy DINS-buffer inventories that used to be listed here are gone
# from this list on purpose: since road-15 those bare names belong to the
# CANONICAL perimeter-frame pages, and qa_maps skips the legacy product itself
# when its perimeter sibling exists. Listing them here would suppress the good
# page, which it did for one run on 2026-09-12.)

# The QA-map landing page. index.html here is the hand-written project landing
# page; qa_maps.py writes qa-maps-index.html, and a filtered run would publish
# an index of only the fires that run happened to rebuild.
qa-maps-index.html

# Landsat damage maps from the corrected `damage_landsat_v2` tables. That
# bundle is the era-check bundle: advisory, not production, and nothing points
# at it. One fire of its hundred arrived here from an unrelated run on
# 2026-09-12 with no page linking to it. Delete this line when the whole set
# is rebuilt and linked from a page that says what it is for.
damage_*_landsat_v2.html

# Superseded by the v5 damage maps beside them. damage_sentinel2_v4 is the
# Carlson-only 66-fire bundle at cut 0.84 and never was the production recipe;
# since road-15 the production bundle has its own 66-fire out-of-fold table, so
# damage_*_sentinel2_v5.html is the current set.
damage_*_sentinel2_v4.html

# The run tag is not part of a fire's name. Since road-15 a canonical
# perimeter-frame product is published under the bare fire id
# (inventory_DINS_2025_EATON.html), and the un-tagged legacy product beside it
# is skipped rather than published. These are the old tagged filenames.
inventory_*__perimeter.html
